 "identity_rules": {
  "canonical_log_identity": "(blockHash, transactionHash, logIndex); blockHash is RECORDED for every log. Only byte-identical repeats of the same identity collapse to one record (refs kept). Two logs with the same (transactionHash, logIndex) but any differing field (blockHash, address, topics, data, blockNumber, transactionIndex) are an UNRESOLVED CONFLICT - even inside finalized B, because it evidences provider inconsistency - and are never counted, never resolved by majority/recency; removed:true logs are kept as explicit removal transitions (added/removed/re-added), a removed-only identity is not a birth; any row holding an unresolved record is NOT known-zero and cannot feed the all-six claim",
  "launch_identity": "(suite_row by log.address == factory, Launched.token, Launched.poolId); birth block b0 = log.blockNumber, creation tx index = log.transactionIndex",
  "ordering": "(blockNumber, transactionIndex, logIndex) ascending; 'earliest' always means this order",
  "first_pool_rule": "downstream classification: a token in more than one Launched log keeps the earliest as birth, later ones are marked additional_pool (retained, not a new launch); a token under two factories is a suite conflict -> both records unknown",
  "cross_check": "hook PoolRegistered for the same poolId in the same tx with creator == Launched.creator; mismatch or absence -> layout_unexpected / partial, never silently accepted",
  "classification_row5_vs_row6": "by emitting factory address only (0x1176... = row 5, 0xb9e5... = row 6); hook address must agree (0x1f91 / 0xdda9); atomic buy presence is NOT a classification criterion; row-6 create selectors/ABI and row-4 ABI stay unknown",
  "exclusions_are_downstream": "quote (Launched.quote: 0x0 = ETH, USDC, crypto majors, stock tokens) and first-pool study-frame filters are evaluator declarations applied AFTER the census; the census keeps every Launched log with its quote",
  "census_vs_downstream": "the census is an exact RAW-EMITTER census: every Launched log is retained with its emitter (factory), quote, token, poolId and identity; first-pool marking (additional_pool), quote classes and study-frame exclusions are DOWNSTREAM evaluator declarations recorded against the retained rows, never dropped at acquisition"
 },
